tml_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","login":"Mickeon","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon"},"body":"Discovering how \"trivial\" it was to make it work, I've already propagated a call to `queue_redraw` in the past, and I kept thinking that a propagating notification would do the trick here, in a more polished way. So the way the PR handles it as of writing seems appropriate to me.\n\nLike, you could argue it's quite inefficient to notify the entire tree for something only a few known nodes need, but let's not cross our bridges before we come to them. It's for debugging purposes, it's fine.\n\nIf you end up struggling implementing the \"synchronize with the debug button\" feature properly, it could be done in a follow-up PR, if you want. Without it, the PR already solves one part of the puzzle.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119816#pullrequestreview-4724595786","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119816","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-07-17T17:10:49Z"},{"id":4841702215,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIJaDRw","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"98904261ab16e679d1dad13f0e55d0c1f4537247","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90930?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/ttencate","id":90930,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTMw","login":"ttencate","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119816#pullrequestreview-4841702215","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119816","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR",